  "title": {
    "en": "Parametric & Vector-Valued Functions",
    "ar": null
  },
  "chapterTag": {
    "variant": "category",
    "className": "ap-tag",
    "badgeClassName": "ap-wt",
    "emoji": "📌",
    "category": "AP Calc BC BC-3 — Parametric & Vectors",
    "weightBadge": "11–12% of exam",
    "topics": [
      "Parametric derivatives & arc length",
      "Vector-valued functions & motion"
    ]
  },
  "content": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "When a curve is traced by a parameter \\( t \\), motion in the plane is captured by component functions and their derivatives.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Parametric calculus",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "\\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} \\). Speed is \\( \\sqrt{(dx/dt)^{2}+(dy/dt)^{2}} \\), and arc length is \\( \\displaystyle\\int\\sqrt{(dx/dt)^{2}+(dy/dt)^{2}}\\,dt \\). A vector position \\( \\mathbf r(t)=\\langle x(t),y(t)\\rangle \\) has velocity \\( \\mathbf r'(t) \\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Slope",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\dfrac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Speed",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\sqrt{x'^{2}+y'^{2}} \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Arc length",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\displaystyle\\int\\sqrt{x'^{2}+y'^{2}}\\,dt \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Velocity",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( \\langle x'(t),y'(t)\\rangle \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example · Parametric slope",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "For \\( x=t^{2},\\ y=t^{3} \\), find \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx} \\). \\[ \\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{3t^{2}}{2t}=\\frac{3t}{2}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Parametric arc length",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Find the arc length of \\(x=t^2,\\;y=\\tfrac{2}{3}t^3\\) from \\(t=0\\) to \\(t=1\\).\\[\\frac{dx}{dt}=2t,\\quad\\frac{dy}{dt}=2t^2.\\]\\[L=\\int_0^1\\sqrt{4t^2+4t^4}\\,dt=\\int_0^1 2t\\sqrt{1+t^2}\\,dt=\\left[\\tfrac{2}{3}(1+t^2)^{3/2}\\right]_0^1=\\tfrac{2}{3}(2^{3/2}-1)=\\tfrac{2(2\\sqrt2-1)}{3}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "A particle moves with \\(x(t)=\\cos t,\\;y(t)=\\sin t\\). Find the speed at \\(t=\\pi/4\\) and the total distance travelled from \\(t=0\\) to \\(t=\\pi\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Speed \\(=\\sqrt{\\dot x^2+\\dot y^2}=\\sqrt{\\sin^2t+\\cos^2t}=1\\) (constant). Distance \\(=\\int_0^\\pi1\\,dt=\\pi\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "quizWidget": {
    "enabled": true
  }
}
